      "message": "Further reading of `man 2 write` suggests inconsistency can be expected as part of the API. So you\u0027re right that a failed write_all_at() should fail the whole operation. But if it\u0027s just the new hash generation that fails, nothing is made inconsistent so we can safely report it as a partially successful write to safely lock in the successful changes that have been made.",
